From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SRX build agent <agent@vyos-srx.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Nov 2026 20:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile.am: skip test suite on emulated mips64el

The test suite (test-cmdline, test-features) drives the built ethtool
binary against real network device names ("devname"). The mips64el
package build runs under qemu-user in Docker with no netdevs, so every
test returns 1 and aborts the build. Skip the test suite.

Note: the patch must modify an upstream source file, not debian/rules:
dpkg-source -b copies the source tree's debian/ (already patched by
--before-build) into its temp dir before applying the patch list, so a
debian/-touching patch gets double-applied ("Reversed patch detected").
---
 Makefile.am | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index 5a61a9a..19f9db9 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -70,3 +70,10 @@ endif
 dist-hook:
 	cp $(top_srcdir)/ethtool.spec $(distdir)
 
+
+# The test suite (test-cmdline, test-features) drives the built ethtool
+# binary against real network device names ("devname"). The mips64el
+# package build runs under qemu-user in Docker with no netdevs, so every
+# test returns 1 and aborts the build. Skip the test suite.
+TESTS =
+check_PROGRAMS =
-- 
2.39.5

